{{!--
  Shot-pattern RESOLUTION card (CP2020 p.109) — posted for a corridor the shooter already aimed, once
  the shot has finished being presented, in place of resolving it unattended. Rendered via
  renderChatCard with
  { weaponName, band, widthM, dmgFormula, shells, multiShell, templateId,
    rows: [{ name, status }], anyRows, rollLine, scatterLine, coverLines, anyCoverLines }.
  `status` arrives PRE-LOCALIZED from JS in THREE states (2026-08-25 soak ruling) — in pattern /
  in pattern behind a rated barrier, naming it and its SP / behind an unrated wall, exempt — so the row
  stays one declarative shape rather than branching per figure. Rows are DIVs for the same reason
  spread-result.hbs uses them: core's layered `ul` styling wins over a module rule on this build, and a
  chat card wants no markers.

  `coverLines` names every rated object the APPLY is going to charge, including one the path merely
  crosses with nobody behind it — the card has to show what the button will do, and a barrier that
  breaks on an empty corridor would otherwise post a chew card out of nowhere. Pre-localized and
  triple-stashed like every other assembled line here.

  `rollLine` and `scatterLine` are PRE-LOCALIZED in JS for the same reason, and each is an EMPTY STRING
  when it does not apply — a payload carrying no attack roll prints neither, and a shot that hit prints
  no scatter. Both carry markup (bold totals, the coloured verdict), so both are triple-stashed.

  The cp-confirm-spread-zone button + data-template-id are verbatim from spread-confirm.hbs — one
  dispatch (damage-hooks.js registerDamageHooks) resolves either card, relays to the active GM, and
  locks the card against a second press. i18n via CPLocal; triple-stash where the string carries <b>.

  cp-clear-spread-zone beside it VOIDS the shot instead of applying it: the pattern is deleted and this
  card is stamped resolved+cleared, after which the render pass in damage-hooks.js swaps this whole
  button row for the cleared line. It is the reason the card can never "go out of date" — the pattern
  is not collected by either expiry clock while this card is still unresolved, so the only two ways a
  pattern ends are the two buttons below.
--}}
<div class="cyberpunk save-prompt">
  <h3>{{CPLocal "SpreadConfirmTitle" weapon=weaponName}}</h3>
  <div class="save-info">
    {{#if rollLine}}<span>{{{rollLine}}}</span><br>{{/if}}
    {{#if scatterLine}}<span>{{{scatterLine}}}</span><br>{{/if}}
    <span>{{{CPLocal "SpreadConfirmSummary" band=band width=widthM dmg=dmgFormula}}}</span><br>
    {{#if multiShell}}
      <span>{{{CPLocal "SpreadConfirmShells" shells=shells dmg=dmgFormula}}}</span><br>
    {{/if}}
    {{#if anyCoverLines}}
      {{#each coverLines}}<span>{{{this}}}</span><br>{{/each}}
    {{/if}}
    <div class="cp-spread-resolve-list">
      {{#if anyRows}}
        {{#each rows}}
          <div class="cp-spread-resolve-row">{{{CPLocal "SpreadResolveRow" name=this.name status=this.status}}}</div>
        {{/each}}
      {{else}}
        <div class="cp-spread-resolve-row">{{CPLocal "SpreadResolveNobody"}}</div>
      {{/if}}
    </div>
    <span class="save-note">{{CPLocal "SpreadResolveBasis"}}</span>
  </div>
  <div class="save-buttons">
    <button class="cp-confirm-spread-zone" data-template-id="{{templateId}}">{{CPLocal "SpreadResolveBtn"}}</button>
    <button class="cp-clear-spread-zone" data-template-id="{{templateId}}">{{CPLocal "SpreadClearBtn"}}</button>
  </div>
</div>
